-    "position_note": "INTERPRETIVE PLACEMENT ON A COMMITTED BLOCK FACE, NOT A RECOVERED LOT (T-0182). EIGHT DOCUMENTED DOCTORS AND NOT ONE OFFICE. A physician's office and apothecary's back room on the Lake Street frontage, where a doctor is found by people who need one. It is left unnamed on purpose: four of the eight are documented households in this dataset and attaching any of them to an invented building would turn a hypothesis into a false attribution. This building does not stand where a centre in the programme put it: it stands on the north face of blk_lake_lasalle, whose line and bearing are read from the block boundary in data/traces/vectors/thompson_lots.json — the same committed geometry the lot grid and the corridor gate are derived from. Its front wall is set 1.50 m back from that lot line, which is the one line every record on this face stands on, and its bearing is the face's own rather than the zero a hand-authored centre carried. What the programme still chooses is where along the face it stands — 80.740 m from the face's west end. IT IS NOT the position it already occupied: this building moved along the street, and the paragraph below says what moved it. WHAT IS INVENTED IS STILL EVERYTHING THAT MATTERS: that a building stood here at all, and that it was this trade's. The dataset's 20 m working georeference uncertainty applies on top of an already invented position, and standing on a derived block face is not standing on a recovered lot. DISPLACED BY AN ATTESTED PLACEMENT, ON THE OWNER'S RULING OF 2026-09-21 (T-0251), AND THE RULE IS GENERAL: where an ATTESTED placement and an INFERRED placement collide on one lot, the attested one stands and the inferred one moves or is withdrawn. first_presbyterian_church is documented at the south-west corner of Lake and Clark and reached the scene off a modern OpenStreetMap kerb, standing 1.90 m out past this block's committed Lake Street frontage line and in the platted roadway; the 3.395 m reconciliation th