SEARCH/hogan_store.md section 5. WORKING UNCERTAINTY ABOUT 20 M, which is the georeference's residual (data/datum.json: 17.5 m RMS on Wright 1834, 3.7 per cent paper stretch), not an additional guess. Facade bearing 180, due south onto Lake Street, which is an inference from the street and not a statement: no source says which way the house fronted, and the corner would equally admit a Dearborn Street front. THE GROUND UNDER IT IS NOW MODELLED: the e1834_harbor_cut heightfield was extended east and its box now runs local E -320..+1700 and N -400..+400 (data/terrain/epochs/e1834_harbor_cut/heightfield.json), so this footprint sits on real terrain and the validator measures its contact rather than clamping at a box edge. It lands within the walker's 0.35 m step-up rule, so the phase carries no ground_contact declaration. That is new as of this parcel: docs/LIBERTIES.md L40 - two thirds of the town standing on ground that had not been built - is already in that document's Resolved section, and this record is written on the far side of that resolution: no Lake Street building in this parcel needed a ground_contact declaration. MOVED BACK ONTO ITS LOT 2026-11-03 (T-3360), on the owner's report of buildings 'placed in the middle of the walkways or alleys': its side wall stood 1.75 m out past the Dearborn Street lot line of blk_south_water_clark, on the plank walk's line; moved 2.25 m back so that wall stands 0.50 m inside the lot line. The translation is dE -2.25 m, dN +0.01 m in local ENU, so UTM E 447760.52 N 4637304.38 becomes E 447758.266 N 4637304.394. NOTHING THE SOURCES SAY MOVED: the corner, side, block or cluster this record is placed by is unchanged, and so is its confidence grade; the coordinate was derived, never read, so it is re-derived against this project's own platted lot line and alley, which tools/check_structure_clearance.py now holds every 1835 building to.",
